<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>62.0</apiVersion>
    <description>Profile engine for intake-driven task generation. On caseman__Intake__c insert, evaluates the new economic-stabilization fields + safety signals and creates Tasks for follow-up patterns.

Profiles (v2):
- If no government ID → "Help apply for replacement ID" (High, +1 day)
- If no health insurance → "Help apply for Medicaid / HIP 2.0" (Normal, +3 days)
- If unemployed AND looking → "Refer to WorkOne + UI with DV exemption" (Normal, +3 days)
- If shelter requested → "Begin shelter intake — confirm bed and prep arrival" (High, today)
- If Risk_Level = High → "Schedule danger assessment within 48h + immediate safety planning" (High, today)
- If no bank account or unsafe joint account → "Help open survivor-only bank account" (Normal, +5 days)
- If childcare needed → "Help apply for CCDF voucher (Indiana child care)" (Normal, +3 days)
- If no/unreliable transportation → "Refer to transportation resources" (Normal, +5 days)
- If no benefits and has children → "Help apply for SNAP + WIC + TANF" (Normal, +3 days)

All tasks are owned by Lana (Director); advocate refines/reassigns as needed. Each task has a deep description with SFTS-specific context so Lana doesn't need to remember the institutional knowledge.</description>
